# DAISY BELL (Harry Dacre, 1892; public domain): the song a computer first sang, Bell Labs on an IBM 704, 1961.
# Melody and harmony read from flutetunes.com's MIDI of the chorus, down a minor seventh from G into her range (A, E3 to E4). Its
# one turn on "mar-" is one note here, and "u-" is added where the sung tune has it (the flute setting rests there).
